From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:43:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Break lines after soft hyphens with a hyphen

`StyleProperty::SoftHyphens` (`TextStyle::soft_hyphens`): CSS `hyphens`.
`Break` by default: the opportunity after a soft hyphen is like any other
and nothing is drawn, as before. `NoBreak` is `hyphens: none`; `Hyphen` has
the advance of the hyphen, which the embedder shapes and draws.

`LineMetrics::hyphen_advance` is the part of a line's `advance` that is the
hyphen. The min/max-content measurer counts the hyphen at the end of the
fragment it ends. A hyphen that does not fit takes an earlier opportunity,
or overflows.
